    "result_text": "Full build passes. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\n`membershipTier` now becomes `GOLD` when the owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3+ members, otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\n## Where the logic lives\n\nThe existing `Owner.getMembershipTier()` computes the individual-based tier (SILVER/BRONZE) from a single owner's own fields \u2014 it can't count household members since an entity has no repository access. The GOLD upgrade is fundamentally a different concern (it depends on how many *other* owners currently share the household), so I placed it at the mapping layer where collaborators are available \u2014 exactly the pattern the codebase already uses for the response-only `bulkSignupWarning` field.\n\n1. **New `HouseholdMembershipTierEvaluator`** (`rest/validation/`) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility component mirroring the existing `BulkSignupWarningEvaluator` / `CityOwnerCounter` / `NamesakeCounter` idiom. Its one method, `qualifiesForGold(householdId)`, returns true when at least 3 owners share the id (null id \u2192 never qualifies). Threshold and tier name are named constants.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.applyHouseholdMembershipTier(...)`** \u2014 a new `@AfterMapping` hook that upgrades the already-mapped tier to `GOLD` when the evaluator says so, leaving the entity's BRONZE/SILVER result in place otherwise. No BRONZE/SILVER logic is duplicated \u2014 it reuses the entity's computation as the base and only supersedes it.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` field description to document the GOLD rule.\n\n## Verification\n- Target test `AcceptanceTest.coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` passes (third household member \u2192 `GOLD`).\n- Full `./mvnw test`: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 0 failures/errors.\n\nI kept everything consistent with the established in-memory-count idiom (streaming `findAllOwners()`), which the transactional test harness sees correctly since all three members are persisted before the GET.",
